Evaluate $integral_0^oo e^(- s^2 - 1 / s^2) d s$

]
#proof(title: "Solution")[
$(s - 1 / s)^2 = s^2 + 1 / s^2 - 2$, let $x = s - 1 / s$ which is increasing on $\(0\,oo\)$ since $0 < s < oo$, $- oo < x < oo$, then $s = frac(x + sqrt(x^2 + 4), 2)$ and #display-equation($integral_0^oo e^(- s^2 - 1 / s^2) d s = e^(- 2) integral_(- oo)^(+ oo) e^(- x^2) (1 / 2 + frac(x, 2 sqrt(x^2 + 4))) d x = e^(- 2) integral_0^oo e^(- x^2) d x = frac(e^(- 2) sqrt(pi), 2)$)

]
