Evaluate $integral_0^oo frac(log x, x^2 + 1) d x$

]
#proof(title: "Solution")[
#display-equation($integral_0^oo frac(log x, x^2 + 1) d x & = integral_(- oo)^oo frac(y e^y, e^(2 y) + 1) d y\
 & = integral_(- oo)^oo frac(y, e^y + e^(- y)) d y\
 & = 0$)

