#statement("Exercise")[
A fully faithful functor $F : cal(C) arrow.r cal(D)$ is injective on objects up to isomorphism

]#label("Fully faithfull functor is injective on objects up to isomorphism")
#proof(title: "Solution")[
Suppose $F\(X\)= F\(Y\)= T$, let $f : X arrow.r Y$ be the map corresponds to $1_T$ in $H o m\(F\(X\)\,F\(Y\)\)$, then $f : X arrow.r Y$ is an isomorphism because we can also let $g : Y arrow.r X$ be the map corresponds to $1_T$ as in $H o m\(F\(Y\)\,F\(X\)\)$, then $F\(g compose f\)= F\(g\)compose F\(f\)= 1_T compose 1_T = 1_T$, thus $g compose f$ corresponds to $1_T$ in $H o m\(F\(X\)\,F\(X\)\)$, but $F\(1_X\)= 1_(F\(X\)) = 1_T$, thus $g compose f = 1_X$, similarly, $f compose g = 1_Y$

]
