Now let's show coimage and image are isomorphic. $f i = 0$ induces $upright(c o k e r) i arrow.r^g B$, claim that $g$ is monic

Suppose $X arrow.r^x upright(c o k e r) i$ is morphism such that $g x = 0$, it induces $upright(c o k e r) x arrow.r^j B$, since $q p k = 0$, $f k = j q p k = 0$ induces $ker q p arrow.r^l ker f$, since $q p$ is epi, $p k = p i l = 0$ induces $upright(c o k e r) x arrow.r^r upright(c o k e r) i$, since $p$ is epi, $p = r q p arrow.r.double r q = 1_(upright(c o k e r) i)$, hence $q$ is monic, $q x = 0 arrow.r.double x = 0$

#align(center)[
#align(center)[#set text(size:7pt)
#diagram(spacing:(7mm,9mm),
node((1,0),[$ker q p$]),
node((0,1),[$ker f$]),
node((1,1),[$A$]),
node((2,1),[$B$]),
node((3,1),[$upright(c o k e r) f$]),
