edge((2,2),(2,1),"->",[$j$]))]
]
$pi f = 0$ induces $A arrow.r^h ker pi$, claim that $h$ is epi

Suppose $ker pi arrow.r^y Y$ is morphism such that $y h = 0$, it induces $A arrow.r^p ker y$, since $q j k = 0$, $q f = q j k p = 0$ induces $upright(c o k e r) f arrow.r^m upright(c o k e r) j k$, since $j k$ is monic, $q j = m pi j = 0$ induces $ker pi arrow.r^s ker y$, since $j$ is monic, $j = j k s arrow.r.double k s = 1_(ker pi)$, hence $k$ is epi, $y k = 0 arrow.r.double y = 0$

#align(center)[
