#statement("Exercise")[
$\[n\]= { 1\,dots.h.c\,n }$, what is the cardinality of ${ f in A u t\(\[n\]\)\|f\(i\)eq.not i\,forall i in\[n\]}$

]
#proof(title: "Solution")[
Consider $A_k = { f in A u t\(\[n\]\)\|f\(k\)= k }$, by Inclusion-exclusion principle #ref(label("Inclusion-exclusion principle"), supplement: none), we have #display-equation($n ! = lr(|union.big_(i = 1)^n A_n|) & = sum_(k = 1)^n\(- 1\)^k sum_(i_1 < dots.h.c < i_k) lr(|A_(i_1) inter dots.h.c inter A_(i_k)|)\
 & = sum_(k = 1)^n\(- 1\)^k binom(n, k)\(n - k\)!\
 & = sum_(k = 1)^n\(- 1\)^k frac(n !, k !)\
$) Thus the probability of picking such an auto morphism is $sum_(i = 1)^n frac(\(- 1\)^k, k !)$ which approaches $e^(- 1)$ as $n$ approaches infinity

]
