#statement("Exercise")[
$phi.alt in "Aut"\(E\)$, $nabla^phi.alt = phi.alt^(- 1) compose nabla compose phi.alt$ is again a connection. Furthermore, $nabla$ is flat $arrow.r.double nabla^phi.alt$ is flat

]
#proof(title: "Solution")[
#display-equation($nabla^phi.alt\(f times.o s\) & = phi.alt^(- 1) compose nabla\(f times.o phi.alt s\)= phi.alt^(- 1)\(d f times.o phi.alt s + f and nabla\(phi.alt s\)\)= d f times.o s + f and nabla^phi.alt s$) Over a local trivialization, $phi.alt s = A s$, then #display-equation($A^(- 1)\(nabla\(A s\)\)= A^(- 1)\(d\(A s\)+ omega and A s\)= A^(- 1)\(d A s + A d s + omega and A s\)=\(d + A^(- 1) d A + A^(- 1) omega A\)s$) Hence the connection form for $nabla^phi.alt$ is $A^(- 1) d A + A^(- 1) omega A$. If $d omega + omega and omega = 0$, then #display-equation($ & d\(A^(- 1) d A + A^(- 1) omega A\)+\(A^(- 1) d A + A^(- 1) omega A\)and\(A^(- 1) d A + A^(- 1) omega A\)\
 & = d A^(- 1) d A + d A^(- 1) and omega A + A^(- 1) d omega A - A^(- 1) omega and d A\
 & + A^(- 1) d A and A^(- 1) d A + A^(- 1) d A and A^(- 1) omega A + A^(- 1) omega A and A^(- 1) d A + A^(- 1) omega A and A^(- 1) omega A\
 & = d A^(- 1) d A + d A^(- 1) and omega A - A^(- 1) omega and omega A - A^(- 1) omega and d A\
 & + A^(- 1) d A and A^(- 1) d A + A^(- 1) d A and A^(- 1) omega A + A^(- 1) omega and d A + A^(- 1) omega and omega A\
 & = d A^(- 1) and\(d A + omega A\)+ A^(- 1) d A and A^(- 1)\(d A + omega A\)\
 & =\(d A^(- 1) + A^(- 1) d A A^(- 1)\)and\(d A + omega A\)\
 & =\(d A^(- 1) - A^(- 1) A d A^(- 1)\)and\(d A + omega A\)\
 & = 0$)

]
#statement("Exercise")[
Suppose $M\,N$ are smooth manifolds of dimension $m\,n$, $f : M arrow.r N$ is a smooth map, $\(x^1\,dots.h.c\,x^m\)$, $\(y^1\,dots.h.c\,y^n\)$ are local coordinates around $p in M$, $q = f\(p\)in N$, then the corresponding matrix of $d f$ with respect to basis $(frac(partial, partial x^1) \, dots.h.c \, frac(partial, partial x^m))$, $(frac(partial, partial y^1) \, dots.h.c \, frac(partial, partial y^n))$ is $(frac(partial y^i, partial x^j))$. In particular, this gives the change of coordinates formula

]
#proof(title: "Solution")[
#display-equation($d f (frac(partial, partial x^i))\(g\)= frac(partial\(g compose f\), partial x^i) = sum_j frac(partial g, partial y^j) frac(partial y^j, partial x^i) = sum_j frac(partial y^j, partial x^i) frac(partial, partial y^j)\(g\)$) According to Exercise #ref(label("Hom(V,W)=V^* tensor W"), supplement: none), $d f = sum_(i\,j) frac(partial y^j, partial x^i) d x^i times.o frac(partial, partial y^j)$, we can define higher differential $d^k f = sum_(i_1\,dots.h.c\,i_k\,j) frac(partial y^j, partial x^(i_1) dots.h.c partial x^(i_k)) d x^(i_1) dots.h.c d x^(i_k) times.o frac(partial, partial y^j)$

]
#statement("Exercise")[
Suppose $omega in Omega^1\(M\)$, $X\,Y in T M$, then $d omega\(X\,Y\)= X\(omega\(Y\)\)- Y\(omega\(X\)\)- omega\(\[X\,Y\]\)$

]#label("Exterior derivative of one form")
#proof(title: "Solution")[
By linearity, we can assume $omega = u d v$, then #display-equation($d omega\(X\,Y\) & = d\(u d v\)\(X\,Y\)\
 & = d u and d v\(X\,Y\)\
 & = d u\(X\)d v\(Y\)- d u\(Y\)d v\(X\)\
 & = X u Y v - Y u X v$) And #display-equation($ & thin thin quad X\(omega\(Y\)\)- Y\(omega\(X\)\)- omega\(\[X\,Y\]\)\
 & = X\(u d v\(Y\)\)- Y\(u d v\(X\)\)- u d v\(\[X\,Y\]\)\
 & = X u d v\(Y\)+ u X\(d v\(Y\)\)- Y u d v\(X\)- u Y\(d v\(X\)\)- u\[X\,Y\]v\
 & = X u Y v + u X Y v - Y u X v - u Y X v - u X Y v + u Y X v\
 & = X u Y v - Y u X v$)

]
