$square.stroked u = 0$ in $bb(R)^(3 + 1)$, $u\(x\,0\)= 0$, $u_t\(x\,0\)= f\(x\)in C^2\(bb(R)^3\)$, show that $integral_0^oo\|u\(0\,t\)\|^2 d t lt.eq C parallel f parallel_(L^2\(bb(R)^3\))$

]
#proof(title: "Proof")[
Hint: $u\(x\,t\)= frac(t, 4 pi) integral_(S^2) f\(x + t w\)d S_w = - frac(1, 4 pi) integral_(S^2) integral_t^oo frac(d, d lambda) f\(x + lambda t\)d lambda$

$u\(0\,t\)= frac(t, 4 pi) integral_(S^2) f\(t w\)d S_w$, $\|u\(x\,t\)\|lt.eq C / t integral_(bb(R)^3)\|nabla f\|d x$

